## RDS — Secrets Manager Managed Password

- RDS uses `ManageMasterUserPassword` — AWS Secrets Manager owns the master password.
- **Rotation is DISABLED** — do not re-enable it without implementing runtime secret fetching first.
  Rotation invalidated the `DATABASE_URL` in Amplify env vars (broke auth on 2026-03-20).

### Check / disable rotation

```bash
aws secretsmanager describe-secret --secret-id "<SECRET_ARN>" --region us-east-2 --profile napx \
  --query '{RotationEnabled: RotationEnabled}'

# If accidentally re-enabled:
aws secretsmanager cancel-rotate-secret --secret-id "<SECRET_ARN>" --region us-east-2 --profile napx
```

### Get current password

```bash
aws secretsmanager get-secret-value --secret-id "<SECRET_ARN>" \
  --region us-east-2 --profile napx \
  --query 'SecretString' --output text | \
  node -e "const s=require('fs').readFileSync('/dev/stdin','utf8'); const p=JSON.parse(s).password; console.log(encodeURIComponent(p));"
```

### After a password change — update Amplify immediately

```bash
# Always fetch ALL current env vars first, patch DATABASE_URL, then write-back the full set.
aws amplify update-app --app-id <APP_ID> --region us-east-2 --profile napx \
  --environment-variables "...ALL_VARS...,DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:<URL_ENCODED_PASS>@<ENDPOINT>:5432/napx_pms?schema=public&sslmode=no-verify"

# Trigger redeploy
aws amplify start-job --app-id <APP_ID> --branch-name <BRANCH> --job-type RELEASE \
  --region us-east-2 --profile napx
```

> **Always URL-encode the password** (`encodeURIComponent()` in Node.js). Characters like `>`, `:`,
> `?`, `[`, `]`, `$`, `#` will silently break the connection string if not encoded.

### TODO: runtime secret fetching (proper long-term fix)

1. Add `secretsmanager:GetSecretValue` to the Lambda execution role (scoped to the secret ARN).
2. Fetch the secret at Lambda cold-start and construct `DATABASE_URL` at runtime.
3. Remove `DATABASE_URL` from Amplify env vars.
4. Re-enable rotation.

